pocket-motion-only: the shutter (0034) is this repository's; no upstream target renders an exposure.

0067 — a declared shutter samples the transform origin between ticks.

0066 made the origin animatable. The shutter evaluates only the props
`integrates` names off the tick, and every other prop keeps the frame's
tick in every sample. Left out, a zoom whose focal point travels — scale
2 held, the origin moving — would render sharp under a shutter while the
same pan written as a translate blurs. The origin is part of the transform,
so its four props join the translate, scale, rotation and skew in
`integrates`; jumps, fills and the hold rule are unchanged.

Guard: `shutter_holds_everything_but_transforms` gains an origin fraction
and an origin length, each read at a half-tick offset (0 -> 0.03125, 8 ->
8.5), and a hue-rotate track that must stay the frame's; red with the origin
left out of `integrates`, and red with HUE_ROTATE put in it. Pocket-motion
`src/anim/timelines.ts`'s `SHUTTER_INTEGRATED` mirrors the list, held to it
by `tests/shutter.test.ts`.

Ledgers: no digest moves — no composition declares both a shutter and an
animated origin, and `shutter-blur`'s 90 frames are what they were.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

diff --git a/engine/core/src/shutter.rs b/engine/core/src/shutter.rs
index 2d4499cd..7be687b7 100644
--- a/engine/core/src/shutter.rs
+++ b/engine/core/src/shutter.rs
@@ -5,10 +5,12 @@
 //! the average of several samples spread over an exposure, and a sample needs
 //! the value between two ticks. This module defines it, narrowly:
 //!
-//! - Only TRANSFORM props are ever evaluated off the tick (`integrates`).
-//!   Opacity, colours, layout and paint props keep the value of the frame's
-//!   own tick in every sample, so a gate stays a gate and a fade reads as it
-//!   does unblurred.
+//! - Only TRANSFORM props are ever evaluated off the tick (`integrates`), the
+//!   transform origin among them (pocket-motion patch 0067): a zoom whose
+//!   pivot travels moves its pixels through both. Opacity, colours, colour
+//!   filters, layout and paint props keep the value of the frame's own tick
+//!   in every sample, so a gate stays a gate and a fade reads as it does
+//!   unblurred.
 //! - Between ticks `n` and `n + 1` the value is the segment's own eased curve
 //!   at the fraction, and ONLY when both ticks sit on one segment that has at
 //!   least one interior tick and whose curve the realm's value at `n + 1`
@@ -44,6 +46,10 @@ pub fn integrates(prop: u8) -> bool {
             | p::ROTATE_X
             | p::ROTATE_Y
             | p::SKEW_X
+            | p::ORIGIN_X
+            | p::ORIGIN_Y
+            | p::ORIGIN_X_PX
+            | p::ORIGIN_Y_PX
     )
 }
 
